Sample:
```
function recordGapHistory() {
  const p = race.player;
  pushHistory(p.history, race.time, playerProgressCapped());
  for (const a of race.ai) pushHistory(a.history, race.time, Math.min(TOTAL_LAPS, a.dist / L));
}
function pushHistory(arr, t, p) {
  const last = arr[arr.length-1];
  if (last && t - last.t < 100) return; // 10Hz
  arr.push({t,p});
  if (arr.length > 4000) arr.splice(0, 500);
}
```
Player progress in standings: need consistent. Currently playerProgress returns `TOTAL_LAPS` when finished, else weird initial formula. AI progress should cap at TOTAL_LAPS when finished. For gaps, use a monotonic "distance covered" measure in laps, including negative initial. Player: p.lapsCompleted + sNorm but initial special: if lapsCompleted===0 && sNorm>0.72 -> sNorm-1. That makes player at grid (behind start line, sNorm ~0.99) progress -0.01, consistent with AI negative dist. Good. AI: a.dist / L can be negative at start (grid). Great, both can be negative and monotonic. Cap at TOTAL_LAPS? For gap purposes when finished, cap both at TOTAL_LAPS. But leader's history for a trailing car: if leader finished, history ends at 3.0. Trailing car's progress < 3, so we can find time when leader was at that progress. Good. If leader finished long ago and trailing car is still on its final lap, gap grows as it should.

Gap lookup:
```
function gapToLeaderSeconds(leader, progress) {
  const hist = leader.history;
  if (!hist.length) return 0;
  // find latest entry with p <= progress? We want time when leader was at `progress`.
  // Progress increasing. Search from end backward for first p <= progress, then next has p >= progress; interpolate.
  let hi = hist.length - 1;
  if (hist[hi].p <= progress) {
    // leader not yet ahead (shouldn't happen); fallback
    return 0;
  }
  let lo = 0;
  // binary search for first index with p >= progress
  while (lo < hi) { const mid = (lo+hi)>>1; if (hist[mid].p >= progress) hi = mid; else lo = mid+1; }
  const b = hist[lo], a = hist[Math.max(0, lo-1)];
  if (a === b) return Math.max(0, (race.time - b.t)/1000);
  const f = (progress - a.p) / (b.p - a.p);
  const tAt = a.t + (b.t - a.t) * clamp(f,0,1);
  return Math.max(0, (race.time - tAt)/1000);
}
```
